.SH NAME
niac-attachment-policy-remove - Withdraw an approval from the policy file


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBniac attachment-policy remove  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Remove one policy from the policy file. Run as root (an elevated shell on
Windows). The argument must match a line of the file exactly as 'list' prints it;
a policy the daemon was given as a flag is not in the file and is removed by
dropping the flag.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for remove


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--storage-keep\fP=500
	Run history records to keep, pruned oldest first on start (0 keeps every run)

.PP
\fB--storage-path\fP=""
	Path to NIAC run history database (default: ~/.niac/niac.db)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  sudo niac attachment-policy remove en16=direct
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBniac-attachment-policy(1)\fP


